n the resulting SDK-shaped record. Metadata is a\ncorrelation aid, not an authorization token. Enforce ownership in your application.",[290,749,751],{"id":750},"binding-behavior","Binding behavior",[286,753,754,755,758],{},"Implement all four ",[298,756,757],{},"CustomerBindings"," methods:",[700,760,761,767,773],{},[703,762,763,766],{},[298,764,765],{},"bind(vatlyId, hostId)"," atomically associates the two IDs.",[703,768,769,772],{},[298,770,771],{},"record(vatlyId)"," records an unattributed customer without clearing an existing binding.",[703,774,775,738,778,781],{},[298,776,777],{},"vatlyCustomerIdFor(hostId)",[298,779,780],{},"hostCustomerIdFor(vatlyId)"," return an ID or null.",[286,783,784,785,788],{},"Enforce uniqueness on ",[322,786,787],{},"both sides"," in the database. Fluent's pre-checks do not\nreplace concurrency-safe constraints. Do not silently reassign an existing binding.\nKeep test and live bindings separate.",[290,790,792],{"id":791},"transactions-belong-to-the-host","Transactions belong to the host",[286,794,795,796,799,800,804],{},"All webhook repositories, bindings, audit records, and outbox writes must join the\ntransaction started by ",[298,797,798],{},"webhookCalls.process(event, work)",". A global transaction\nvariable shared between concurrent requests is not safe. Use your database's\ntransaction context or request-scoped drivers. See ",[801,802,803],"a",{"href":255},"webhooks"," for the\ndeduplication algorithm and reaction matrix.",[286,806,807,808,397],{},"For remote resource fields, use the ",[801,809,813],{"href":810,"rel":811},"https:\u002F\u002Fdocs.vatly.com\u002Fapi-reference",[812],"nofollow","API reference",[815,816,817],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .s7zQu, html code.shiki .s7zQu{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-default-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-d